# Knowledge Assets

Files in `docs/` are governed Knowledge Assets — containers for meaning, not casual notes. Use `templates/knowledge-assets/KNOWLEDGE_ASSET_TEMPLATE.md` as a starter structure; templates are draft, not governed assets.

For capture routing and promotion discipline, see `docs/operations/OPM-002_KNOWLEDGE_CAPTURE_WORKFLOW.md` (Draft / Advisory). Do not over-promote observations into formal assets.

For decision promotion and approval, see `docs/operations/OPM-003_DECISION_PROMOTION_APPROVAL_WORKFLOW.md` (Draft / Advisory).

## Placement

Place new assets in the appropriate `docs/` subfolder per `docs/README.md`.

## Required metadata

Add or update YAML front matter when creating or substantially revising formal assets:

```yaml
---
knowledge_asset_id: ACR-001
title: Human-readable title
classification: Concept Record  # Concept, Decision, Governance, Product, etc.
status: Exploratory             # Exploratory | Draft | Proposed | Approved | Canonical | Superseded | Retired
authority_level: Informational  # Informational | Advisory | Canonical | Governing
owner: John S. Villasenor
last_updated: 2026-07-05
---
```

Seed assets may lack full metadata; add it on the next substantive edit.

## Every asset must answer

- Why it matters
- Who owns it
- Whether it is authoritative
- What decisions it informs
- What context would be lost without it
- How future agents should use it

## Status and promotion

- Do not set **Approved** or **Canonical** without explicit Founder approval
- **Curator** may recommend; only **Founder** approves during foundation phase
- Backlog questions are not decisions; lessons and research notes are evidence, not decisions
- **Proposed is not Approved**; do not use **Exploratory** status on Decision Records
- When superseding an asset, update its status and link the replacement
- Keep exploratory content clearly labeled until promoted

For ID prefixes, status models, and authority hierarchy, see `asset-authority.mdc` and OLY-GOV-002.
